WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.568 --> 00:00:18.608
Mary was so tired that she went to bed right after supper.

2
00:00:19.889 --> 00:00:23.250
In the middle of the night, she was awakened by dreadful sounds.

3
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.371
Someone was crying and screaming at the same time.

4
00:00:27.391 --> 00:00:30.252
"It's Colin," she said.

5
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.640
"He's having a tantrum.

6
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.441
He sounds hysterical!"

7
00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:39.202
She suddenly understood why people always gave in to him.

8
00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:43.804
Anything was better than listening to these horrible, sobbing screams.

9
00:00:45.204 --> 00:00:46.184
She was terrified.

10
00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:49.605
But at the same time, she was angry.

11
00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:52.446
"Somebody ought to make him stop!"

12
00:00:52.906 --> 00:00:53.506
she cried.

13
00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.188
Just then she heard a person running down the corridor.

14
00:00:59.468 --> 00:01:01.429
Her door opened, and the nurse came in.

15
00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:06.792
"He's worked himself into hysterics," the nurse said breathlessly.

16
00:01:06.812 --> 00:01:09.514
"He'll do himself harm.

17
00:01:10.894 --> 00:01:12.375
No one can do anything with him.

18
00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:15.137
You must come and try to help him.

19
00:01:15.197 --> 00:01:15.957
He likes you."

20
00:01:17.778 --> 00:01:19.379
Mary flew down the corridor.

21
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.782
The closer she got to Colin's room, the angrier she grew.

22
00:01:25.122 --> 00:01:27.724
She threw open the door and ran to Colin's bed.

23
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:29.920
"Stop it!"

24
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.421
she shouted at him.

25
00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:34.041
"Everybody hates you!

26
00:01:34.061 --> 00:01:38.583
I wish everybody would run away and let you scream yourself to death!"

27
00:01:40.343 --> 00:01:45.265
A nice, sympathetic child would never have thought such things, never mind said them.

28
00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:49.246
But it was the best possible thing for Colin to hear.

29
00:01:50.566 --> 00:01:53.627
He had been lying on his stomach, beating his pillow with his hands.

30
00:01:54.927 --> 00:01:59.081
But at the sound of Mary's furious voice, he turned around suddenly.

31
00:02:00.723 --> 00:02:05.106
His face was red and swollen from crying, and he was gasping and choking.

32
00:02:06.488 --> 00:02:07.628
Mary did not care.

33
00:02:07.648 --> 00:02:13.253
"If you scream another scream," she threatened, "I'll scream too.

34
00:02:14.254 --> 00:02:16.936
I can scream louder than you can, and I'll frighten you."

35
00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:19.478
"I can't stop!"

36
00:02:20.259 --> 00:02:21.080
Colin gasped.

37
00:02:22.481 --> 00:02:23.862
He was shaking all over.

38
00:02:23.882 --> 00:02:25.183
"I can't!"

39
00:02:26.956 --> 00:02:27.676
"You can!"

40
00:02:28.157 --> 00:02:28.937
shouted Mary.

41
00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:33.260
"Most of what's wrong with you is your temper and hysterics.

42
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.862
Just hysterics, hysterics, hysterics!"

43
00:02:38.303 --> 00:02:41.104
She stamped her foot each time she said the word.

44
00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:45.427
"I felt a lump," choked out Colin.

45
00:02:45.447 --> 00:02:47.648
"I'll be a hunchback.

46
00:02:48.408 --> 00:02:49.449
I'm going to die."

47
00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.752
He turned on his stomach again and began to sob, but he didn't scream.

48
00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.281
"Nurse!" Mary commanded.

49
00:02:58.301 --> 00:03:01.103
"Come here and show me his back."

50
00:03:02.484 --> 00:03:03.565
The nurse, Mrs.

51
00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:08.488
Medlock, and Martha had been standing together near the door, watching her deal with Colin.

52
00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.251
More than once they had gasped with fright.

53
00:03:12.271 --> 00:03:16.493
"Perhaps he won't let me," said the nurse.

54
00:03:18.415 --> 00:03:18.935
"Show her!"

55
00:03:19.475 --> 00:03:20.136
said Colin.

56
00:03:20.156 --> 00:03:22.437
"Then she'll see."

57
00:03:23.918 --> 00:03:25.840
What a poor, thin back it was.

58
00:03:27.244 --> 00:03:30.746
Every rib could be counted and so could every bone of the spine.

59
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:36.368
But Mary did not count them as she bent over his back and studied it solemnly.

60
00:03:37.788 --> 00:03:40.049
Everyone in the room waited breathlessly.

61
00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.791
"There's not a single lump there," Mary said at last.

62
00:03:44.811 --> 00:03:47.913
"The only lumps are backbone lumps.

63
00:03:49.253 --> 00:03:51.534
And you can only feel those because you're so thin.

64
00:03:52.855 --> 00:03:56.296
Mine used to stick out just as much as yours until I started getting fatter."

65
00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.702
"I didn't know that he thought he had a lump on his spine," said the nurse.

66
00:04:01.722 --> 00:04:05.885
"His back is weak because he refuses to sit up."

67
00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:09.087
Colin lay still for a minute.

68
00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.649
Huge tears streamed down his face and wet the pillow.

69
00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.351
He felt so relieved.

70
00:04:17.451 --> 00:04:19.493
Finally he spoke to the nurse again.

71
00:04:19.513 --> 00:04:22.714
"Do you think I could live to grow up?"

72
00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:28.121
"You probably could, if you do what you're told and go outside often."

73
00:04:29.721 --> 00:04:31.582
Colin's tantrum had left him weak.

74
00:04:32.842 --> 00:04:36.363
He put out his hand toward Mary, and she reached over and took it.

75
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:38.864
"I'll go out with you, Mary.

76
00:04:40.084 --> 00:04:46.426
I won't hate fresh air if we can find He stopped himself just before saying the secret garden.

77
00:04:46.446 --> 00:04:50.687
"I'd like to go out if Dickon would come and push my wheelchair.

78
00:04:51.907 --> 00:04:55.248
I very much want to see him and the fox and crow."

79
00:04:56.864 --> 00:04:59.745
The nurse plumped up Colin's pillow and remade his bed.

80
00:05:01.065 --> 00:05:02.966
Then she brought tea to Colin and Mary.

81
00:05:02.986 --> 00:05:08.267
"He'll need to sleep soon," she said just before she left them alone.

82
00:05:08.287 --> 00:05:11.068
"Would you like me to sing to you?"

83
00:05:11.588 --> 00:05:12.248
asked Mary.

84
00:05:12.268 --> 00:05:16.309
"What I'd really like is to hear more about the secret garden.

85
00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.850
Did you notice I almost mentioned it?

86
00:05:20.431 --> 00:05:21.951
Have you found out any more about it?"

87
00:05:23.271 --> 00:05:24.172
Mary hesitated.

88
00:05:24.192 --> 00:05:25.532
"I think I have."

89
00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.681
"Oh, if I could go there, I think I could live to grow up.

90
00:05:30.921 --> 00:05:33.682
What do you think it looks like?"

91
00:05:33.702 --> 00:05:35.062
"Well Mary gulped.

92
00:05:35.082 --> 00:05:38.884
"I think everything has grown into a lovely tangle.

93
00:05:39.984 --> 00:05:42.905
There are probably lots of roses just starting to wake up.

94
00:05:44.945 --> 00:05:49.887
I think daffodils and snowdrops and lilies are working their way out of the ground.

95
00:05:51.187 --> 00:05:54.008
Maybe there are clusters of purple and gold crocuses."

96
00:05:55.464 --> 00:05:58.149
She looked over at Colin, who had fallen asleep.

97
00:05:59.532 --> 00:06:05.483
"And perhaps," she said softly, "perhaps the robin has found a mate and is building a nest."
